  body: |
    # Exceptional LCW circumstances and substantial risk

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes circumstances in which a claimant without sufficient assessment points is treated as having LCW, including specified disease conditions or substantial risk to a person’s health.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 42310 retains a work-related exclusion and separate disease/evidence conditions. Substantial risk is assessed from the evidence and circumstances under 42320 onwards; it is not established by a condition label, a low score or anxiety alone. No medical assessment is made here.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 42310, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=38)
    - [DMG 42315, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=38)
    - [DMG 42320, PDF page 39](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=39)
    - [DMG 42322, PDF page 39](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=39)
    - [DMG 42323, PDF page 39](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e5ff8a8c9f882ae5997f4c/dmgch42.pdf#page=39)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

